---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import StackTerminal from '../components/StackTerminal.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/Timeline.astro';
import ContactCard from '../components/ContactCard.astro';
---

<PageLayout title="About" description="António Barbosa — designer, developer, tinkerer.">
  <style>
    .hero { padding: 4rem 0 3.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 4rem; }
    .name-small { font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gray); display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .name-big { font-size: clamp(4rem, 12vw, 9rem); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 0.88; color: var(--gray-light); margin: 0 0 2rem; }
    .hero-tagline { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--gray); max-width: 420px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }
    .hero-tagline strong { color: var(--gray-light); }

    .bio-text p { font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--gray); margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .bio-text p:last-child { margin: 0; }
    .bio-text strong { color: var(--gray-light); font-weight: 600; }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .name-big { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 14vw, 6rem); }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="hero">
    <span class="name-small">António Barbosa</span>
    <h1 class="name-big">KASTICO</h1>
    <p class="hero-tagline">
      <strong>Designer turned developer</strong> from Portugal.
      Building software by day, obsessing over custom setups by night.
    </p>
  </div>

  <StackTerminal />

  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <span class="section-label">Story</span>
      <div class="bio-text">
        <p>I've spent most of my life in front of a computer — gaming, coding, designing, producing. It started with a family PC, a PS2, and an illegally downloaded copy of GTA Vice City that introduced me to the modding community. I was 8 or 9, replacing car textures and tweaking variables. That obsession with <strong>making things your own</strong> never left.</p>
        <p>After studying Graphic Design at <strong>ESAD.CR</strong> and a programming course at <strong>CENCAL</strong>, I landed at a small company building their own business software. My focus is UI/UX and visual identity, but in a small team you end up doing everything — backend, deployment, the works.</p>
        <p>I'm convinced that's the best way to start a career: learn everything, build versatility, understand the full stack of how things actually work.</p>
        <p>Today I work mainly in <strong>C++ with Qt</strong> at Softpack, building cross-platform apps for Linux, Windows, macOS and Android. I built a kitchen display system from scratch, worked on migrating our apps from Qt 5 to Qt 6, and created a reusable QML component library, plus <strong>DataGrid</strong>, an open-source component you can find on my GitHub. On the side I'm exploring Zig and embedded, and slowly making peace with JavaScript frameworks.</p>
        <p>I'm a terminal guy. GUI is fine. But the terminal is power. You won't change my mind.</p>
      </div>
      <ContactCard />
    </div>

    <aside class="sidebar-sticky">
      <div class="sidebar-block">
        <span class="sidebar-label">Info</span>
        <ul class="meta-list">
          <li><span>Location</span><span class="meta-val">Portugal</span></li>
          <li><span>Role</span><span class="meta-val">Software Developer</span></li>
          <li><span>Focus</span><span class="meta-val">UI/UX · Full-stack</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <Timeline />
      <div class="sidebar-block">
        <span class="sidebar-label">Links</span>
        <ul class="meta-list">
          <li><span>GitHub</span><a href="https://github.com/kastico" target="_blank" style="color:var(--accent-light);font-size:0.82rem;">kastico</a></li>
          <li><span>Twitter</span><a href="https://x.com/_kastico" target="_blank" style="color:var(--accent-light);font-size:0.82rem;">_kastico</a></li>
          <li><span>Mastodon</span><a href="https://m.webtoo.ls/@kastico" target="_blank" style="color:var(--accent-light);font-size:0.82rem;">@kastico</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</PageLayout>